# Scene of the Crime: "{T}, Tap an untapped creature you control: Add one mana of any color." On turn 3 Bot1 controls no creature (Bot2's Ornithopter is not
# Bot1's) so the ability is refused; once Bot1 casts its own Ornithopter (summoning sick, tapping it is the cost not its {T} ability, CR 302.6) it taps it
# for red mana, which casts a Lightning Bolt at Bot2. The Scene and the Ornithopter are then both tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Scene of the Crime
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Scene of the Crime.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Scene of the Crime.Activate(Ability: Tap an untapped creature)
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Scene of the Crime.Activate(Ability: Tap an untapped creature; Tap: Ornithopter; Color: Red)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
[Bot1.Main2]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Scene of the Crime.Activate(Ability: Tap an untapped creature)

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Scene of the Crime.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
